            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Governments can influence healthy dietary choices of populations by taxing relatively unhealthy foods and drinks and/or subsidizing relatively healthy options. Experimental and modelling studies have shown that such fiscal policies can contribute to the prevention of diseases such as obesity.</AbstractText>
